# Responsive Layout — Phone Portrait & Tablet Landscape

Target **phones (portrait)** and **tablets in landscape**. Device rotation is locked that way via `app_orientation.dart`. Do not redesign existing POS billing/dashboard layouts unless explicitly asked.

## Breakpoints

Use shared constants (e.g. `AppBreakpoints`), not magic numbers:

| Name   | Width        | Intent                          |
|--------|--------------|---------------------------------|
| mobile | `< 600`      | Single column, full-bleed feel  |
| tablet | `>= 600`     | Wider content, optional 2-col   |

Prefer `LayoutBuilder` for local decisions; use `MediaQuery.sizeOf(context)` only when the whole screen width matters. On tablets, prefer `shortestSide >= 600` for device class (orientation-independent).

## Mobile (default)

- Single-column layouts
- Comfortable edge padding (e.g. 16–20)
- Bottom nav / primary actions thumb-friendly
- Full-width primary buttons
- Avoid horizontal scroll for core content

## Landscape Tablet

- Use width: side rails, two-pane workspaces, or wider content planes
- Forms may use 2-column field rows and a higher max-width than phone
- Cap narrow reading content when it helps; do not stretch tiny phone UI awkwardly
- Same design tokens; only structure/spacing density may change
- Existing POS (billing two-pane, dashboard side rail) already follows this — leave alone unless asked

```dart
// ✅ GOOD
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    final isTablet = constraints.maxWidth >= AppBreakpoints.tablet;
    return Center(
      child: ConstrainedBox(
        constraints: BoxConstraints(maxWidth: isTablet ? 960 : double.infinity),
        child: content,
      ),
    );
  },
);

// ❌ BAD — hardcoded MediaQuery everywhere, different APIs per device
if (MediaQuery.of(context).size.width > 500) { ... }
```

## Shared Rules

- One responsive decision point per screen (helper or `LayoutBuilder`), not scattered `if (width)` checks
- Same design tokens on both sizes; only structure/spacing density may change
- Test both mobile portrait and tablet landscape when building or changing screens
- Safe areas: respect notches / system bars with `SafeArea` where needed
